    burden: "Small intestine cancer accounts for 3.8% of digestive system cancers in the United States (NCI); adenocarcinoma, neuroendocrine tumours, lymphoma and GIST each make up a share. SEER estimates 14,450 new cases and 2,170 deaths in the US in 2026, and five-year relative survival of 71.8% for people diagnosed from 2016 to 2022, all types combined.",
