    burden: "Rare in most high-income countries: under one case per 100,000 men per year in the United States (NCI) and about one in the United Kingdom (GLOBOCAN 2024, age-standardised). Rates are several times higher in parts of southern and eastern Africa and South America (GLOBOCAN 2024: Botswana 8.1, Bolivia 3.2, Uganda 2.9, Paraguay 2.1 per 100,000), tracking HPV prevalence, phimosis and low circumcision rates.",
